22. STRICT PROHIBITIONS

Do not:

- Hardcode a single sample question.
- Hardcode endpoint names.
- Hardcode one JSON payload for every module.
- Assume every angle is an inclination to HP or VP.
- Assume every question supplies true length.
- Treat OCR text as a mathematically validated solution.
- Allow the LLM to invent missing measurements.
- Treat zero as the default for unknown values.
- Use regex alone as the semantic interpretation engine.
- Use keyword matching as the only module classifier.
- Use prompt-only logic where deterministic validation is required.
- Generate a static drawing unrelated to the actual question.
- Return plausible-looking answers without constraint validation.
- Mark unsupported modules as fully implemented.
- Silently discard ambiguities.
- Rewrite unrelated working functionality.
- Expose secrets or execute untrusted generated code without appropriate safeguards.
- Claim testing succeeded without running tests.

Regex, rules, and pattern matching may support OCR cleanup, entity extraction, and known terminology. They must not be the sole mechanism for understanding every question.

